Subject: util: make CNTFRQ_EL0 reads survive binary translators
Why: sysinfo.cpp evaluates the TSC frequency in a static initializer that
 executes `mrs cntfrq_el0` raw; the Android emulator's arm64 translator
 (ndk_translation 0.2.2) does not implement the register and kills the
 process with SIGILL at library load ("Undefined instruction 0xd53be008").
 Add utils::get_cntfrq_safe(): reads CNTFRQ_EL0 under a scoped SIGILL
 handler and, when it faults, calibrates CNTVCT_EL0 against
 CLOCK_MONOTONIC (rounded to 10kHz). Route the static initializer and
 init_arm_timer_scale() through it.
Upstream-status: candidate

diff --git a/rpcs3/util/asm.hpp b/rpcs3/util/asm.hpp
index 008aaa0..ee6eca2 100644
--- a/rpcs3/util/asm.hpp
+++ b/rpcs3/util/asm.hpp
@@ -198,9 +198,8 @@ namespace utils
 
